  "course_description": "Third-year-level course given in French. Intensive study of written French based on syntactic and lexical analysis of a variety of texts. Work on clear expression and control of the fine points of French grammar. Bi-weekly compositions with extensive revisions and concern for the process of writing in a foreign language.",
  "course_notes": "Required course materials: Krueger and Fauvel, _Tâches d'encre: French Composition_, 5th ed. ISBN: 978-0-357-65888-8. Assessment: engaged participation, six staged formal essays, three short presentations, other small writing assignments and language exercises. Prerequisites: French 203, a score of '4' or '5' on the French AP exam, or equivalent experience.",
